  "description": "#5057 — `undo_op`, the ref-addressed undo, and the fixture that proves the `On` convention. An `OpRef` is `(device_id, seq)` and the two runners mint their own device ids, so until now no fixture could name one and the five ref-addressed undo commands were all unaddressable. `On` resolves to the n-th op the fixture has appended, 1-based, exactly as `Cn` names the n-th op-created block. The point of the ref form over the positional one is that it survives a newer op landing after the target (#2446), which is what the second edit here is for: a depth-0 positional undo would take it instead.",
